WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.890
- I have four piles of
mushrooms right here,

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.809
so I'm gonna be here for a minute.

00:00:03.809 --> 00:00:04.928
- (Producer) You can
use the food processor.

00:00:04.928 --> 00:00:06.720
- Wait, there's a food processor?

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.256
Yes! I would love to use
the food processor, please.

00:00:10.256 --> 00:00:12.157
(laughing)

00:00:12.157 --> 00:00:15.990
(exciting music playing)

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:16.823
Hey, what's up?

00:00:16.823 --> 00:00:19.140
My name is Tway and
welcome to Making it Big,

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.040
the show where I turn your
favorite food and make it giant.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.320
I have a very special
guest with me here today,

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.333
Mr. Ben Hundreds.

00:00:28.606 --> 00:00:29.439
- Hi Tway.

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:32.070
- Hi, thank you so much for being here.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:32.910
- Thank you for having me.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.550
- I'm really nervous about this challenge

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.370
because I mean by the looks
of the bamboo steamer,

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.890
I kind of know what you're
gonna challenge me to.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.300
But I don't know what kind.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.596
So let's see.

00:00:43.596 --> 00:00:45.450
- [Ben] Bánh.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.120
- [Tway] Of course, it's a soup dumpling.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.256
The hardest one to make.

00:00:50.256 --> 00:00:51.089
- You really think so?

00:00:51.089 --> 00:00:52.440
- Yes, absolutely.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.520
Soup dumplings?

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.240
It's incredibly difficult
to make, just this size.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.860
- I really wanted to challenge you today.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.360
- How big do you want me to make this?

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.470
- I want big.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.400
- Like how big?

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.290
- Like I want to carry it, like this big.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.760
- Oh, you wanna like hug it?

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.593
- Yeah.

00:01:06.593 --> 00:01:07.650
- That's a really big challenge, dude.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.750
You couldn't just like
challenge me to make

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.244
like a gyoza or something?

00:01:11.244 --> 00:01:13.200
- No, I could have, but I didn't want to.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.550
- I accept your challenge.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.400
I will make a giant soup dumpling.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.573
Let's get started.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.860
For soup dumplings, we need to make soup.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.320
So, I'm gonna be using
an Instant Pot for this.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.900
This is my chicken
stock that's gonna go in

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.390
Then adding some flavor to it.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:35.220
So soy sauce, some ginger,
garlic, green onions.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.170
And this is a little cheat code.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.760
This is ham.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.930
It's going to add some
nice flavor to the broth

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.930
without having to add
some actual bones into it.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.730
Give this a nice little stir.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.234
This is probably the easiest
part of the soup dumpling, so

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:53.730
The dumpling is shaped like a purse

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.170
which I think is really cute.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.003
That's a cute purse.

00:01:56.003 --> 00:01:58.410
Can you edit a purse, a
dumpling purse for me?

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.810
And the more pleats
that you have at the top

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:04.050
that means whoever's making
your dumpling is very skilled.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:07.470
So today I'm gonna try my
best to make as many pleats

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:08.303
as possible.

00:02:08.303 --> 00:02:11.064
Maybe like a hundred, maybe less.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.173
We'll see, this looks
like it's going to be done

00:02:13.173 --> 00:02:16.833
so I'm gonna strain it
and then add my gelatin.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.700
This smells so good.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:21.690
So, so good.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:22.680
I think it's the ham

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.370
and the soy that is giving
this really savory smell.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.320
I wish I can drink this right now,

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.630
but I have to bloom my gelatin.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.710
This is actually not the
traditional way of making it.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:37.950
I'm using gelatin because I'm
making a big giant dumpling,

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.470
so I don't want to risk it not setting.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:43.590
And I also can't just
add this gelatin right

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.060
into the hot water.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.670
I have to bloom it with cold water,

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.810
because hot water is
going to kill the gelatin.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.310
Meaning it's not gonna help it bloom.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.800
Then I'm gonna strain it.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.450
Look at that color.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:58.950
You can tell just by looking

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.490
at it that it has so much flavor.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.220
Pour this right into my sheet tray.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.840
This is going to take four hours,

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:10.143
so in the meantime, I'm
going to make my dough.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.160
Usually dumpling dough
is really easy to make.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.440
I usually use all purpose flour,

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:19.650
but since this is a big giant dumpling,

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.430
I'm going to use bread flour
and cake flour instead.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.440
Bread flour has more gluten, so I feel

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.320
like it has more structure
to hold the dumpling better.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.940
Five and a half cups of bread flour

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.250
and then cake flour will keep it tender.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.970
Little salt, give it all a whisk.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.100
Then I have hot water.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.688
So the bread flour I'm just kind of taking

00:03:40.688 --> 00:03:42.150
an educated guess.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.790
I'm not sure how this
is going to turn out.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.440
I hope that it will hold

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.800
up like I thought it would, but we'll see.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:50.633
Okay,

00:03:50.633 --> 00:03:53.490
time to get messy.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:56.790
So my first time ever
having soup dumplings

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.220
was here in America.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.860
I don't think there's any
soup dumplings in Vietnam.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:04.020
Maybe now since it's so popular.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.630
And the first time I had a soup dumpling,

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:10.590
I burned my mouth 'cause I just
didn't know what to expect.

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:12.870
But the flavor, it was insane.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.200
I've never had anything
juicier, and I was hooked.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.670
I'm gonna put it out on the table

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:20.640
and then knead it until it turns smooth.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.360
So usually when I make dumplings,

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.260
the dough is probably half this size.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:31.200
And it makes like 50 dumplings.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.440
But this is the dough for one.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.260
This is probably gonna
take me a hot minute.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.290
My arms are actually feeling
really good, feeling strong.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:42.480
If you hate the gym, get in the kitchen.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:45.390
So in culinary school, making dough

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:49.410
we actually had to fight over the mixer.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.140
There were only like four to a class,

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.980
so most of us had to do this by hand.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.467
I'm getting flashbacks.

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.640
This dough feels pretty good.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.833
All I need to do is check.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.680
Yep, and it bounces back.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.513
So it's ready.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:10.383
My baby's gonna rest for 30 minutes.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.820
This is

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.720
five pounds of pork.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.090
That's a lot of meat for one dumpling.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.260
So let's get to it.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:20.940
I have some scallions here.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:22.500
So for the scallions, I'm using

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.750
both the whites and the greens.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.020
It both offers a really
nice texture to the filling.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:31.440
I love the smell of just raw green onions.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.680
And this goes right into the pork.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.860
Then I have some baby portobella's here

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.293
that I'm just going to mince up.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.890
Oh, I'm just kidding.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:48.270
Okay. This is a product of one mushroom.

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:50.040
I have four piles of mushrooms right here.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.290
So, I'm gonna be here for a minute.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.790
(peppy music)

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:58.362
(record skipping)

00:05:58.362 --> 00:06:00.030
Wait, there's a food processor?

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:03.758
Yes. I would love to use
the food processor, please.

00:06:03.758 --> 00:06:05.640
(laughing)

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:10.640
Okay. Four pounds of minced
baby portobella mushrooms,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.920
courtesy of my bestie,
the food processor later.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.950
I'm gonna add it straight into the meat.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:20.730
And I love mushrooms because
it has a natural umami flavor

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:23.010
to it, and it has a meaty texture.

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:24.210
And then for my seasoning,

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:27.810
I'm going to add in soy
sauce, shaoxing wine,

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:31.710
little bit of sesame oil,
salt and white pepper.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:34.233
About like a full bulb of garlic here,

00:06:34.233 --> 00:06:37.080
that I'm just going to grate.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.450
This is pretty much the
amount of garlic I put

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:43.530
in my regular dumpling filling
anyways, cause I love garlic.

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:44.520
Ben is a foodie,

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.800
so I really hope that he likes garlic.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.720
But if he doesn't, then I guess I'll have

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.820
a really big dumpling to myself.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:52.740
And then now I'm gonna grate some ginger.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:56.760
It's great in dumplings,
great in dumping sauce.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.370
What is a dumpling without some ginger?

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:01.230
This is my favorite part.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.420
Time to mix it all together.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.860
All of this is filling
for just one dumpling.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.600
Like this is actually kind of insane,

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.100
and I'm kind of concerned

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:14.250
if it's actually gonna
cook all the way through.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:15.296
But hey,

00:07:15.296 --> 00:07:17.040
(meat mushing)

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:20.271
that's what good pork
dumpling fillings sounds like.

00:07:20.271 --> 00:07:22.770
Okay, I'm kind of avoiding this

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:25.620
because this is the moment of truth.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:28.860
It's assembly time, meaning
I have to roll the dough out,

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:33.293
put this bad boy in the
dough, and then try to pleat.

00:07:33.293 --> 00:07:34.126
(fast instrumental music)

00:07:34.126 --> 00:07:38.190
Now I have all of my components
and I'm ready to assemble.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.800
I actually had to take this part out.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:44.360
This right here, the
bottom of this one out.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:48.780
This is too shallow for
the big dumpling to sit in.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:52.890
So this gives it a nice deep wall,

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.750
so it can hold up the big dumpling.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.750
I'm going to line this first.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.160
I have napa cabbage here.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.530
I'm going to just line the bottom

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:04.260
and the sides so the
dumping doesn't stick.

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:08.730
I'm just kind of working with
hopes and dreams over here.

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:12.810
Okay, I'm gonna dust my surface
so my dough doesn't stick.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:14.220
Roll out my dough.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:19.220
I'm gonna roll this out
into a nice, thin circle.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:23.040
I thought this dough was going
to be harder to roll out,

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.471
but it's actually not because it's

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:28.890
very stretchy, very hydrated.

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:33.840
Now I'm gonna measure this,
18 inches in diameter.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:38.840
Time to transfer this
dough into my basket.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:43.097
(suspenseful instrumental music)

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:46.350
Okay so far,

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:47.610
so good.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:49.980
Now, I'm gonna add this filling.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:52.050
Man, this smells so good.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:56.340
This is just an insane amount
of filling for one dumpling.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.560
I really, really hope that all

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.120
of this pork gets cooked.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.690
And I hope that my dough doesn't fall

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:07.050
apart on me, some way somehow.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:08.520
This is a tricky one.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.170
Okay, all my meat is in.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:13.380
So I'm making a little
well in my meat mixture

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:17.070
so I can put the soup
into the soup dumpling.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:19.890
This is gelatin soup
and this is actually how

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.740
they put the soup into the soup dumpling.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:24.063
Look at that!

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:26.103
Well, I love it.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:30.810
Brushing some water onto
my dumpling wrapper so

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:33.960
when I start to pleat it,
it can stick together.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.450
I'm gonna start right here
because it kind of looks

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.220
like a little pleat right here already.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.900
So I'm just gonna grab.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:43.740
So the more pleats,
means the more skilled.

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:45.390
Let's see if I can get a
hundred. (record skipping)

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.280
I'm on my fifth pleat.

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:50.430
Just trying to be as gentle as possible.

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:53.070
The small pleats aren't
really working out for me,

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:58.070
so I think I might just, I
gotta just do the bigger pleats.

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.840
I didn't get a 100 pleats.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:03.210
I got about like 14.

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:06.180
Not skilled, but not

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:10.200
as bad as I thought it would be.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:13.200
There's a little bit of extra dough here.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.480
I'm just gonna snip it off.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:17.040
See, aesthetic.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.660
Okay, this looks good.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:19.830
Hold this back.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.900
I really, really hope this works.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:23.460
No going back now.

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:25.740
(grunting) Oh man.

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:28.440
I'm gonna put the basket in this.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:31.110
I have boiling water ready for me.

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:34.020
Get this bad boy up here.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:38.079
And I'm gonna let this
steam for two hours.

00:10:38.079 --> 00:10:39.240
(fast instrumental music)

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:42.720
So while my dumpling is steaming away,

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.940
I'm going to start on my sauce.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:46.830
I have some ginger right here

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:49.350
that I'm just gonna cut into thin slices.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:53.790
Perfect. The ginger really
gives the sauce a nice aroma

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.230
and just flavor.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:58.170
Now I have black vinegar
and soy sauce here.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:01.590
I like to add a little
bit more black vinegar

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:02.580
than soy sauce.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:05.610
Usually people like to do equal parts,

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:08.850
but I love my sauce to be (mouth clicking)

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:09.990
very acidic.

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:13.320
And I'm just gonna
measure it with my heart.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:16.140
This reminds me of,
and two shots of vodka.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:17.640
(mouth bubbling)

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:20.340
And then I have a little
bit of chili flakes here.

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:22.770
This is not just some
regular old chili flakes.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:25.470
This is thai chili, chili flakes.

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:28.770
I'm gonna let this sit so the
flavors can start to develop

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:30.330
and marry with each other.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:31.320
That's it.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.903
Two hours later.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:38.820
Dude, Ben is gonna freak out.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.070
This looks really good.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:43.688
Let's plate this and get it ready for Ben.

00:11:43.688 --> 00:11:45.090
(intense music)

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:47.640
Okay. My heart is actually racing

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.710
because I cannot wait to show Ben this.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.993
Ben! I have something for you.

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:53.910
Welcome back.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:54.750
- Wow.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:55.950
- Are you ready?

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:57.879
- I don't know if I am.

00:11:57.879 --> 00:11:59.550
(intense music)

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:00.495
- [Ben] Oh my God.

00:12:00.495 --> 00:12:02.700
You really made a giant soup, oh my god.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.260
- [Tway] Compared to..

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:06.630
- [Ben] Wow. How did you do this?

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:07.650
It's so good.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:09.180
- [Tway] So much trial and error.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:12.270
I think this has to be the
most challenging challenge yet.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:16.213
So this is a total of five pounds of meat.

00:12:16.213 --> 00:12:17.100
- [Ben] Okay.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:19.463
- [Tway] Four pounds of
mushrooms in the filling.

00:12:19.463 --> 00:12:20.296
- [Ben] Wow.

00:12:20.296 --> 00:12:22.860
- [Tway] And the dough by
itself is three pounds.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:25.350
I got us some boba straws.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:28.440
I thought it would be
fun for us to kind of

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:29.580
just drink the soup.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:30.413
- Sure.

00:12:30.413 --> 00:12:31.431
- Let's do it.

00:12:31.431 --> 00:12:34.710
(mouth sipping)

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:35.543
Thoughts?

00:12:35.543 --> 00:12:36.376
- I love it.

00:12:36.376 --> 00:12:38.880
- Okay. Should we dig into this?

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:40.320
- Yes. Yes, we should.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.580
- [Tway] The only way to go about this

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:42.900
is to cut it like a cake.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:43.733
- Sure.

00:12:43.733 --> 00:12:46.226
- [Tway] Would this be
considered like a meat pie now?

00:12:46.226 --> 00:12:48.330
- [Ben] Yeah. (laughing)

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:50.100
- Insane.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:52.140
Okay. I low-key was worried

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:54.720
that it might not be cooked
through, but we're good.

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:55.860
It's cooked through.

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:56.730
- It's perfect.

00:12:56.730 --> 00:12:59.550
- Yes. So this is just
a regular dumping sauce

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:02.280
soy sauce, black vinegar, ginger

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.380
and then we have some chili over there.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:05.213
- Great.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:08.100
- Wow.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:09.750
- [Ben] It tastes like a soup dumpling.

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:10.583
- [Tway] Perfect.

00:13:10.583 --> 00:13:11.986
- It checks out almost all the boxes.

00:13:11.986 --> 00:13:13.740
The biggest difference between this

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:16.290
and a small one is, when
you bite into a small one

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:17.820
it explodes in your mouth.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:18.718
- Right.

00:13:18.718 --> 00:13:19.551
- And like half the time

00:13:19.551 --> 00:13:20.384
you might even burn your mouth

00:13:20.384 --> 00:13:21.542
when you eat a soup dumpling right?

00:13:21.542 --> 00:13:22.375
- [Tway] Exactly.

00:13:22.375 --> 00:13:24.720
- [Ben] So besides that,
it's pretty spot on.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:26.891
- That's because you just
don't got a big enough mouth.

00:13:26.891 --> 00:13:28.110
- Yeah. Maybe.

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:29.982
Can you imagine if I
would've picked it and

00:13:29.982 --> 00:13:30.815
(Tway laughing)

00:13:30.815 --> 00:13:33.570
- [Tway] I think I checked
off all of all the boxes,

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:34.404
to be honest.

00:13:34.404 --> 00:13:35.880
- Okay. I'll give it to you.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.230
- Thank you, thank you.

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.490
Well this has been really fun.

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:40.500
Thank you so much for challenging me.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:43.530
I can officially say that I made a big

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:45.690
soup dumpling. In the comments down below,

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:49.161
let me know what I should make big next.

00:13:49.161 --> 00:13:51.661
(happy music)

